 2. 🚦Blue wave, yellow light 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Tuesday's Democratic election sweep could tap the brakes on the autonomous vehicle industry's ambitious growth plans, Axios mobility expert Joann Muller writes .

 🗣️ The industry's hopes for federal legislation overriding state and local rules "just became a pipe dream," said Rob Grant, AV policy expert and co-founder of Autnmy AI. 🏛️ The big picture: Congress has tried and failed for nearly a decade to establish national rules for autonomous vehicles.

 Although early bills attracted bipartisan support, Democrats lately have opposed industry-backed proposals, citing concerns about safety, labor protections and whether federal regulations should override state laws. If Congress can't pass an AV bill, that will put more stress on state-level policy debates, notes MIT research scientist and mobility expert Bryan Reimer.

 And AV and robotaxi companies were already running into policy roadblocks in several Democratic-led states, including New York, Illinois, Oregon and Massachusetts. Read more 

 
 
